00:12:38,941 --> 00:12:44,300
Speaker 1: So, there are four independent operating scenarios causing the problem.

231
00:12:46,261 --> 00:12:58,319
Speaker 1: One of them is a bug in some BIOS code and microcode that caused the CPU to basically get too much voltage, especially when it was idle and not doing that much.

232
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:15,239
Speaker 1: There was another bug in an algorithm inside of the microcode that would cause the CPU to request too much voltage, which would then change in average somewhere, which then caused the voltage minimum to slowly creep up, which would just cause it to increasingly send more and more voltage to the CPU.

233
00:13:17,142 --> 00:13:19,817
Speaker 1: There was one other issue that's similar to those two.

234
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:31,039
